    {
      "name": "migrate_user_pda",
      "docs": [
        "Grow a historical `UserPda` (48, 80, or already-96 bytes) to the current layout.",
        "",
        "Layouts (exact sizes only):",
        "- 48: disc + 5×u64 (no owner) → backfill `owner`, stamp vesting defaults",
        "- 80: disc + owner + 5×u64 → preserve owner/counters, stamp vesting defaults",
        "- 96: current layout → idempotent rewrite (no field changes)",
        "",
        "Parses by raw size before any realloc so an 80-byte body is never read as the",
        "48-byte struct (which would treat pubkey bytes as deposited/withdrawn/…).",
        "Permissionless and idempotent."
      ],
      "discriminator": [
        48,
        210,
        9,
        164,
        3,
        26,
        140,
        9
      ],
      "accounts": [
        {
          "name": "payer",
          "docs": [
            "Funds rent top-up for reallocation. Deliberately separate from `user` so a stranded",
            "legacy record can be repaired by anyone: a legacy `UserPda` fails to deserialize in",
            "every other instruction, so requiring the owner's signature leaves a wallet that",
            "never comes back permanently unable to deposit, withdraw or claim."
          ],
          "writable": true,
          "signer": true
        },
        {
          "name": "user",
          "docs": [
            "from this key, so writing it into `owner` cannot hand one wallet's record to",
            "another — a caller can only ever repair the record belonging to the key they pass."
